[Theorem 1 (\cite{ciech2021},Theorem 2.6) of arXiv:2605.13512, '2605.13512'] Recall \eqref{microLPT}. Let $c(x,y)$ be a macroscopic speed function which satisfies Assumptions \ref{ass:c} and \ref{ass:c2}, and let ${\bf v} =(x,y) \in \R^2_+$. Define ${\bf v}_n = (\ce{nx}, \ce{ny})$. Then we have the scaling limit
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty}n^{-1}G^{(n)}_{{\bf 0}, {\bf v}_n}= \Gamma_c({\bf v}) = \Gamma_c(x,y)\quad \P-\text{a.s.}
\end{equation}
where $\Gamma_c(x,y)$ is upper-semicontinuous on $\R_+^2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:interior_intersection_right_first of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $a_1 >0$, $p \in (0,1)$. Suppose that we have the setup of Section~(se:bubble_setup of the paper) with $(D,x_0,y_0) = (\delta\mathbf{D},-i\delta,i\delta)$. Let $z_1,z_2,w_1 \in \partial B(0,\delta/2)$ (where $z_1=z_2$ is allowed). Let $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_2}$ (resp.\ $\eta_{z_2}^{\theta_2}$) be the angle $\theta_2$ flow lines starting from $z_1$ (resp.\ $z_2$), stopped upon exiting $B(0,3\delta/4)$. Let $\eta_{w_1}^R$ be the angle $-\pi/2$ flow line starting from $w_1$, stopped upon exiting $B(0,3\delta/4)$. Let $\eta_{w_1}^L$ be the angle $+\pi/2$ flow line starting from $w_1$, stopped upon hitting $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_2}$ or exiting $B(0,3\delta/4)$ (whichever occurs first). In case $\eta_{w_1}^L$ intersects $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_2}$ in $B(0,\delta/4)$, let $\overline{w}$ denote the intersection point, and let $\overline{\eta}^R$ be the angle $-\pi/2$ flow line starting from $\overline{w}$, stopped upon exiting $B(0,\delta/4)$. In case $\overline{\eta}^R$ and $\eta_{z_2}^{\theta_2}$ intersect, sample the internal metric in the regions bounded between them. 
Let $E^p$ be the event that the following hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item $\eta_{w_1}^L$ intersects the left side of $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_2}$ with an angle difference of $-3\pi/2 - \theta_2$, and they do not intersect in any other way.
\item The right side of $\overline{\eta}^R$ and the left side of $\eta_{z_2}^{\theta_2}$ intersect with an angle difference of $-\pi/2 - \theta_2$, and they do not intersect in any other way.
\item There exist $x',x,y,y' \in \eta_{z_2}^{\theta_2} \cap \overline{\eta}^R$ such that $(x,y) \in \intptsapproxbubble{U_{x',y'}}{\epsilon}$ as in~(equation eq:intpts_bubble of the paper) and $U_{x',y'} \subseteq B(0,\delta^{1+a_1})$ and $\metapproxacres{\epsilon}{U_{x',y'}}{x}{y}{\Gamma} \geq \median{\epsilon}+\epsilon^{-a_0}\mathbf{a}_{\epsilon}$.
\item The following event has conditional probability at least $p$ given $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_2}$, $\eta_{z_2}^{\theta_2}$, $\eta_{w_1}^R$, $\eta_{w_1}^L$, $\overline{\eta}^R$, $X_\delta^{\theta_2}$, $X_\delta^{-\pi/2}$, $X_\delta^{+\pi/2}$, and the values of $h$ on these sets:
\begin{itemize}
\item The flow line $\eta_2$ merges into $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_2}$ before entering $B(0,\delta/4)$, and then (in case $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_2}, \eta_{z_2}^{\theta_2}$ do not merge) into $\eta_{z_2}^{\theta_2}$ before entering $B(0,\delta/4)$ the next time.
\item The extension of $\overline{\eta}^R$ merges into the right side of the extension of $\eta_{w_1}^R$ after both exit $B(0,3\delta/4)$.
\end{itemize}
\end{itemize}
Then $\mathbf{P}[E^p] = O(\delta^{{\alpha_{\mathrm{apr}}}})$ as $\delta \to 0$.

