$$|D^{V,T}_t - D^{V,T}_s| \leq \frac{1}{c} \frac{1}{T^\delta} \int_0^{Tt} H^{(T)}(Y_2^T(r)) dr = \frac{1}{c} (D^T(t) - D^T(s)), $$
where $c$ is as in \eqref{assump:H_V_tail}, so, in view of the tightness criterion of \cite[Theorem 7.3]{billingsleySndEdition}, the claimed tightness is implied by the tightness of $D^T$, $T\geq 1$, 
\item[(ii)] By Lemma \ref{lem:cv_ratio_dv_d} and Slutsky's Lemma, ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:320ab241225d80056a127f4756ffd0c13c7e6d583577b5638895f1a0333b1115","revision_digest":"sha256:d6fe3e6a05b410752b9c495c9a5972ed45cc2a296906263a525e82245920f3b0","source_id":"arxiv:2512.01483","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

