[Theorem thm.IIC of arXiv:2411.19145, 'On the intersection of critical percolation clusters and other tree-like random graphs'] Let $\mathcal C_\infty$ be the IIC of Bernoulli percolation on $\mathbb Z^d$, either with $d>6$ and sufficiently spread-out lattice,  or $d>10$ in the nearest neighbor model. There exist positive constants $C$ and $\kappa$, such that for any $\varphi : \mathbb Z^d \to [0,\infty)$,  satisfying  $\|g_{d-4} * \varphi\|_\infty \le 1$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\left[\exp\left(\kappa \cdot \sum_{x\in \mathcal C_\infty} \varphi(x)\right)\right] \le 1+C \, \|\varphi\|_1.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if $d\ge 9$ and $\widetilde {\mathcal C}_\infty$ denotes an independent copy of $\mathcal C_\infty$, then
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb E\left[\exp\left(\kappa \cdot|\mathcal C_\infty \cap \widetilde {\mathcal C}_\infty|^{1-\frac 4d}\right)\right] <\infty.  
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] A spin model $\left< \cdot \right>_{G}$ satisfies Pfaffian relations 
    on $W \subset V$ if and only if for each non-planar pair $(A,B)$, we have
    \begin{equation}
	    \E [ \vp^+(A) \vp^-(B) ] = 0.
    \end{equation}

