{"artifact_digest":"sha256:e22bc878f7974957c3ec345fb1369cb5b13f29595938e2607abfbbf552a7ffbf","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/e2/e22bc878f7974957c3ec345fb1369cb5b13f29595938e2607abfbbf552a7ffbf.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:043de0320d225d81cf01f1c00882b747ce76b6b92148de1b44e1edd49b621b00","bundle_entry_key":"2607-22438-lemma-3-hprime-monotone","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_078","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_078.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2607-22438-lemma-3-hprime-monotone","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Formula \eqref{eq.h'} gives the symmetry. Let \(s=\log(t/(1-t))\). Then \(t>1/2\) is equivalent to \(s>0\), and
\begin{equation*}
 h'(t(s))=
 \alpha\frac{\cosh^2(s/2)}{\cosh^2(\alpha s/2)}.
\end{equation*}
Thus, we obtain
\begin{equation*}
 \frac{\dd}{\dd s}\log h'(t(s))
 =\tanh\left(\frac s2\right)-\alpha\tanh\left(\frac{\alpha s}{2}\right)<0,
 \qquad \text{for }s>0 \text{ and }\alpha>1.
\end{equation*}
