[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2510.27451, 'Bi-martingale optimal transport and its applications'] Let us be given two measures $\mu,\nu \in \mathcal{P}_1(\R)$ on the real line with the same barycentre, $[\mu] = [\nu]$. Then, 
	\begin{equation}

		\rho = \mu \vee \nu := (\FF_\mu \vee \FF_\nu) ''
	\end{equation}
	is a solution of the optimal convex dominant problem \eqref{eq:conv_dom} for  any convex cost function $f:\R\to\R \cup \{+\infty\}$ such that  $\inf \eqref{eq:conv_dom} < +\infty$.

	Moreover, if $f$ is strictly convex, then the solution $\rho = \mu \vee \nu$ is unique.

