\begin{align}
\lambda(t)=\lambda(0)+\int_{0}^{t}{\mathbb R}(y(t),\Psi){\rm d} t + \int_{0}^{t}\Pi_{\lambda(s)}{\rm d} W^{Q}(s)
\end{align}
makes sense with respect to the seminorm ${\mathbb E}\norma{\cdot}_{{\rm BL}}^{2}$.

