[Lem 49 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Suppose that there are $y_1$ strings equal to $s_i$ among $\widehat {\mathbf a}_i$.
        Then for all $\widetilde{\mathbf a}\in \cS^p_{\geq_{\lex}s_i}(m,y_{p,i}-y_1)$, we have
        \begin{equation}

            \mu_{\mathbf a_i} \lt( \widehat{\mathbf a}^{\rem,m}_i=\widetilde{\mathbf a}| \widehat{\mathbf{a}}^m_i \rt)  
            = 
            \frac{ \nu_{\mathbf a_i, \widehat{\mathbf a}^m_i}(\widetilde{\mathbf a})}
            {\sum_{\widetilde{\mathbf a} \in \cS^p_{\geq_{\lex}s_i}(m,y_{p,i}-y_1)} \nu_{\mathbf a_i, \overline{\mathbf a}^m_i}(\widetilde{\mathbf a})},
        \end{equation}
        where
        \begin{equation} 
            \nu_{\mathbf a_i, \widehat{\mathbf a}^m_i}(\widetilde{\mathbf a})=\prod_{t=1}^{K-1}\prod_{j=1}^{m}\frac{ \overline n_{\widetilde{s}_j[t]}^{(t),m,\rem}-\sum_{i<j} 1_{\widetilde{s}_i[t]=\widetilde{s}_j[t]}}{N-n_l^{(1)}+j}.
        \end{equation}
        For all $\widetilde{\mathbf a}\in (\cS^p_{\geq_{\lex}s_i})^m \setminus \cS^p_{\geq_{\lex}s_i}(m,y_{p,i}-y_1)$, we have $\mu_{\mathbf a_i} \lt( \widehat{\mathbf a}^{\rem,m}_i=\widetilde{\mathbf a}| \widehat{\mathbf{a}}^m_i \rt)=0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem Upper bound of cumulants GUE of arXiv:2411.11341, 'Ultra high order cumulants and quantitative CLT for polynomials in Random Matrices'] Let $\mathcal{X}\sim $ GUE or GOE. Consider the polynomial $P(\mathcal{X},\mathcal{D})$ in ((def of P of the paper)) and the random variable $\mathbf{X}$ defined in ((object of the paper)). Suppose that $\mathbf{C}_1$ is satisfied. 
Then there exists a constant $\theta_1\equiv \theta_1 (K, M, t)\in (0, 1)$ such that 
\begin{align}|K_r(\mathbf{X})|\leq \frac{r!^{\frac{M}{2}}}{(\theta_1 N)^{r-2}}, 
\end{align}
for any $N$ and $r\geq 3$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

