body:
[Defn of arXiv:2411.09988, 'A Study in Markov Chains, Loop-Erased Random Walk and Loop Soups'] A discrete-time \textit{(time-homogeneous) Markov chain} on $A$ is a sequence of random variables $X_0, X_1, X_2, . . .$ taking values in a countable (finite or countably infinite) state space $A$ that satisfies the following \textit{(time-homogeneous) Markov property}:
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
\mathbb{P}\{X_{n+1} = y \mid & X_0 = x_o,\ldots,X_n = x_n\}\\
& = \mathbb{P}\{X_{n+1} = y \mid X_n = x_n\}\\
& = \mathbb{P}\{X_{1} = y \mid X_0 = x_n\}.
\end{split}
\end{equation*}

