For this purpose, for any positive integer $n$,  set $\hat{X}:=X^{n+1}-X^n$ for $X=Y,Z,K$. By a similar analysis as Eqs. \eqref{e1} and \eqref{e2}, choosing $a=\frac{1}{2}+4(\lambda+2\lambda^2)$, ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:d8129adbd25d09f7cd6ca1c7fa3bcf3a2731029a5134edf33ad2c5da756b2655","revision_digest":"sha256:dd31351e0c650850208258f061ad43b48ba1093467cd68150b5591e7fb7f7b64","source_id":"arxiv:2605.15781","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

