    By Corollary (cor_bounded_st_times of the paper), it is enough to consider stopping times \(\tau\) satisfying \(\tau\le\tau_{-x, \, y_x^*}\) a.s. Such stopping times have finite expectation, since the exit time of \(Y_y(\cdot)\) from a bounded interval has finite expectation.
    For any such stopping time $\tau$, applying Itô's formula to \(\widehat U(Y_y(\tau))\) in the generalized form valid for functions with absolutely continuous first derivative (see, e.g., [BMSC]), gives
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{split}
