[Lemma lem:ball-calibration of arXiv:2608.31043, 'Sharp constants for weak estimates of Riesz Potentials when $0<s<\min\{n,2\}$'] $e_R$ belongs to $\dot H^{s/2}(\mathbb{R}^n)$ and
\begin{equation*}
 \mathcal{E}_s(e_R)=M_R.
\end{equation*}
If $u\in\dot H^{s/2}(\mathbb{R}^n)$ and $u=1$ almost everywhere on $B_R$, then
\begin{equation*}
 \mathcal{E}_s(z)=M_R+\mathcal{E}_s(u-e_R)\geq M_R.
\end{equation*}
Consequently,
\begin{equation*}
 \operatorname{Cap}_s(B_R)=M_R.
\end{equation*}

