  \begin{equation}
\mathcal{F}=\sigma\left( (\omega(i),\omega_t(i)), \: i\in A\cup B\cup T\right). 
\end{equation}
Using that $F$ and $G$ are $S$-increasing and applying Lemma~(lem:Holley of the paper) to $(\omega,\omega_t)|_S$ , we obtain the following inequality of random variables:
  \begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}[F(\omega,\omega_t)G(\omega,\omega_t)|\mathcal{F}]\geq \mathbb{E}[F(\omega,\omega_t)|\mathcal{F}]\mathbb{E}[G(\omega,\omega_t)|\mathcal{F}]\quad{\text{a.s.}}
