[Definition Def: eff leaves of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] The \emph{effective cherries} 
		of a decorated binary tree $\rho\in{\mathcal T}_b$ are the pairs of edges that share a common parent such that
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item either both edges end with a leaf whose decoration is not $0$
			\item or the left edge stems from the root and ends with a leaf.
		\end{enumerate}

