[Theorem 1 (Root law and multi-root factorization) of arXiv:2607.13210, 'Punctured Wilson--Evolving Sets and Root Identities for Massive Kirchhoff Forests'] Let $x,r\in V$. If $(S_t)_{t\geq0}$ is the ordinary evolving set in $V$ started from
$S_0=\{x\}$, then, we find :
\begin{equation}
  \Pp\bigl(\rho_q(x)=r\bigr)
  =\frac{\pi(r)}{\pi(x)}
  \Pp_{\{x\}}\bigl(r\in S_{T_q}\bigr).
\end{equation}
Consequently, one gets:
\begin{equation}
  \Ee\bigl[\pi(B_q(r))\bigr]=\pi(r).
\end{equation}
More generally, let $x_1,\ldots,x_k$ be distinct vertices of $V$ and set
\begin{equation*}
  A_0=\emptyset,
  \quad \forall i \in [[1,k]]\,,\quad 
  A_i=\{x_1,\ldots,x_i\},
  \quad \text{and}\quad 
  D_{i-1}=V\setminus A_{i-1}.
\end{equation*}
Then, one finds:
\begin{equation}
  \Pp(x_1,\ldots,x_k\in\Root)
  =\prod_{i=1}^k
  \Pp^{D_{i-1}}_{\{x_i\}}
  \bigl(x_i\in S_{T_q}^{D_{i-1}}\bigr).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

