[Lemma 8 (Coefficient asymptotics at an exponential singularity) of arXiv:2607.07712, 'Parameter-Space Heat Flow, Gaussian Density Ratios, and Sharp Hermite Truncation Rates'] Let \(\beta>0\) and \(\lambda>0\). Then, as \(m\to\infty\),
\begin{equation}
[z^m]\,
(1-z)^{-\beta}
\exp\!\left(
\frac{\lambda z}{1-z}
\right)
\sim
\frac{1}{2\sqrt\pi}\,
\lambda^{\frac14-\frac\beta2}\,
m^{\frac\beta2-\frac34}
\exp\!\left(
2\sqrt{\lambda m}-\frac{\lambda}{2}
\right).

\end{equation}

[Prop geographic ineq coupling map of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $\underline u=(u^1,\ldots ,u ^N)\in \widetilde{\mathcal{W}}_n^N$ be such that $\underline u^i:=F_n(u^i)\neq(e,\ldots,e)$ for all $i$, and $\underline v= (\underline u^1,\ldots, \underline u^N)$. Then, for all $w\in \Psi_{N,n, T}(\underline u)$, we have
	\begin{equation}

		d_{\mathrm{LP}}(L[\underline u],L[w])\leqslant \frac 1N\sum_{i=1}^N\Big(h\Big(\frac{N|\underline u^i|}{|\underline v|}\Big)+h\Big(\frac{|\underline u^i|}{n}\Big)\Big)+ 2h\Big(\frac{|\underline v|}{T}\Big).
	\end{equation}

