[Proposition prop:Wick of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Assume the set-up and conditions of Proposition~(prop:underline_comp of the paper) with the only differences that we additionally fix $n\in\mathbf{N}$, consider $j\in[n]$ instead of $j\in[2]$ and do not assume that $x_1\le x_2$. It holds that
\begin{equation}

\mathbf{E}\prod_{i=1}^n\langle G_i-\mathbf{E} G_i\rangle=\sum_{P\in \Pi_n}\prod_{\{i,j\}\in P}\!\!\mathcal{M}_{ij}+\mathcal{O}_\theta\left(\frac{N^{\xi}}{\sqrt{N\eta_*}}\prod_{i=1}^n \frac{1}{N\eta_i} \right),\quad\mathcal{M}_{ij}:=\mathcal{M}\big((x_i,\eta_i,z_i),(x_j,\eta_j,z_j)\big),
\end{equation}
uniformly in the same sense as explained below (equation eq:Cov_UV of the paper). Here $\Pi_n$ denotes the set of all pairings of $[n]$. We use the convention that $\Pi_n=\emptyset$ if $n$ is odd. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

