[Lemma nb_paths of arXiv:2606.09488, 'The temporal stochastic block model'] For all $u,v \in V$ and for all $\ell \in {\mathbb N}$,
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
{\mathbb E}[X_\ell] &\leq  \frac{n (\log n)^\ell }{\ell!} \times (\boldsymbol{a}^T \cdot \Lambda^\ell \cdot \boldsymbol{1}), \\
{\mathbb E}[Y_\ell(u)] &\leq \frac{(\log n)^\ell }{\ell!} \times (b_{\sigma(u)}^T \cdot \Lambda^\ell \cdot \boldsymbol{1}),\\
{\mathbb E}[Z_\ell(u,v)] &\leq \frac{(\log n)^\ell }{a_{\sigma(v)}n\ell!} \times (b_{\sigma(u)}^T \cdot \Lambda^\ell \cdot b_{\sigma(v)}),
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
where $(b_i)_{i \in [k]}$ is the canonical basis of $\mathbb{R}^k$ and $\boldsymbol{1} = (1,\ldots,1)^T \in \mathbb{R}^k$.

