body:
[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Herbst Argument (Proposition 2.14, \cite{massart2003})}


    Let $X \sim \nu$ where $\nu$ is a probability measure on $\R$. Suppose there exists $v \in (0, \infty)$ \st{} for all $\lambda > 0$ it holds that $\ent[\nu]{\exp(\lambda X)} \leq \frac{\lambda^2v}{2} \E[\exp(\lambda X)]$. Then, for every $\lambda > 0$ we have
    \begin{align*}
        \E[\exp(\lambda (X-\E[X)])] 
        \leq \exp\Parent{\frac{\lambda^2v}{2}}. 
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem estimate of arXiv:2503.22334, 'Probabilistic analysis of optimal multi-pivot QuickSort'] For all $0 \le L<\infty$ exists an $M_L<\infty$ such that for all $\lambda \in [-L,L]$ and all $n \ge 0$ we have
    \begin{align}
        \E{e^{\lambda X_n}} \le e^{\lambda^2 M_L}.
    \end{align}

