[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2605.30030, 'Critical exponents for planar random-cluster model with cluster-weight~$q=4$'] There exist constants~$C,c>0$ such that for every~$\eps \geq \delta >0$ and every~$x,y\in \mathbb R^2$ with 
$|x|/16 \geq |y| \geq 4\eps$,
\begin{align*}
 \Ll|\widetilde\pi_2^\delta(x,y,\eps)-\widetilde\Delta^\delta(x,y,\eps)\Rr|
 \le C\, \widetilde\pi_2^\delta(x,y,\eps)\Ll(\tfrac{|y|}{|x|}\Rr)^c+C\,\pi_1^\delta(\eps,|y|)^4\Ll(\tfrac{\eps}{|y|}\Rr)^c   + o_\delta(1).
\end{align*}

