[Definition 8 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] The Markov renewal potential associated with $q$ is the kernel sequence $\psi$ defined by

\begin{equation*}
\psi_k(x,A)=\sum_{n\geq0}q^{(n)}_k(x,A).
\end{equation*}

When $q$ is strict, this sum is finite for each fixed $k$. In general it is interpreted as a non-negative kernel, possibly sigma-finite.

[Lem 11 of arXiv:2608.21090, 'Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process conditioned to have restricted $L_2$-norm'] Let $t_0>0$ and $y>0$. Then, for any Borel-measurable subset $D$ of $\CC([0,t_0])$, it holds for any $T\geq t_0$
    \begin{align}
        \P_x(U\in D~\vert~Z_T\leq y)=\E_x\left[\1_{U\in D}~\frac{\P_{U_{t_0}}\left(Z_{T-t_0}\leq y-Z_{t_0}\right)}{\P_x(Z_T\leq y)}\right].
    \end{align}

