[Lemma lem:C_reg of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Let $\Omega$ be defined as in Theorem~(theo:main of the paper). Fix (small) $c_0,\varepsilon>0$. For any $f_1,f_2\in H_0^{2}(\Omega)$ and $x_j,x_j'\in [c_0,1]$, $j=1,2$, it holds that
\begin{equation}
\left\vert C^{(G)}\big((x_1,f_1),(x_2,f_2)\big) - C^{(G)}\big((x_1',f_1),(x_2',f_2)\big)\right\vert \lesssim \left(|x_1-x_1'|+|x_2-x_2'|\right)^{1/2-\varepsilon} \prod_{j=1}^2\|\Delta f_j\|_{L^2(\Omega)},

\end{equation}
where the implicit constant depends only on $c_0$ and $\varepsilon$.

