{"artifact_digest":"sha256:cc4054cd7ebc0deb487f28610df184a56e870dd20f2ec7717a68aeaf11e392fb","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/cc/cc4054cd7ebc0deb487f28610df184a56e870dd20f2ec7717a68aeaf11e392fb.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:f61be465555ac3a132622a9c82e2b35eb2af784a41a62d060269d26732bbc556","bundle_entry_key":"2606-28869-theorem-15-it-o-is-to-marcus-as-sums-are-","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_038","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_038.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-28869-theorem-15-it-o-is-to-marcus-as-sums-are","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: \emph{(a) Segment.} For a straight segment $\gamma(t)=p+tz$, $t\in[0,1]$, one has $\,\mathrm{d}\gamma=z\,\,\mathrm{d} t$ and
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Sig}^k(\gamma)=z^{\otimes k}\!\int_{0<t_1<\cdots<t_k<1}\!\,\mathrm{d} t_1\cdots\,\mathrm{d} t_k=\frac{z^{\otimes k}}{k!},
\end{equation}
hence $\mathrm{Sig}(\gamma)=\exp_{\otimes}(z)$.

\emph{(b) Chen.} The chord path $X^{\mathrm{PL}}$ concatenates constant pieces, whose signature is $\mathbf 1$, with the chords of increments $z_a$. By Chen's identity and reparametrization invariance,
\begin{equation}
