satisfies Condition (condition-g function of the paper).
Then, for every $n\in \mathbb{N}$ and every  $t \in [0,T]$, the following identities hold $\mathbb{P}$-almost surely,
\begin{align}
\sum_{s\in [0,t]} g(\Delta \langle {u}_n(s), \phi \rangle)
&=\int_0^t \int_{Y} g\bigl(  \ip{P_n F(s,{u}_n(s-),y)}{\phi}{H}\, \bigr) {\eta}(\mathrm{d} s,\mathrm{d} y),

	\end{align}
and
