[Definition 13 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Entropic Stability (Definition 29, \cite{chen:eldan2022})}


    Let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $\R^n$ and $\epsilon > 0$. For all $v \in \R^n$ let $\mathcal T_v\nu$ be its exponential tilt defined through $\frac{d\mathcal T_v \nu(x)}{d\nu} \propto \exp(v\T x)$. The measure $\nu$ fulfills $\epsilon$-entropic stability \wrt{} $\psi : \R^n \times \R^n \to (0, \infty)$ if 
    \begin{align*}
        \psi\Parent{\int_{\R^n} x d\mathcal T_v\nu(x), \int_{\R^n} x d\nu(x)}
        \leq \epsilon \operatorname{D}_{KL}(\mathcal T_v \nu || \nu),
        \quad \text{for all} \quad 
        v \in \R^n. 
    \end{align*}

[Lem 81 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] We have
	\begin{align}
\rmh^0_{\bspi}(\pi) & = \inf\Big\{\rmh^0_{\bspi}(\phi):\ \phi \in \bigcup_{k \ge 1}\ol{\S_k(\pi)}\Big\} \\
&= \inf_U\limsup_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{d_n}\log \bbP(\pi_n \in U) ,
\end{align}
where the infimum on the second line runs over all q-neighbourhoods of $\pi$.  The analogous formulas hold if `$\rmh^0$' is replaced with `$\ul{\rmh}^0$' and `$\limsup$' is replaced with `$\liminf$'.

