body:
[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $X $ have density $f$ with respect to $\pi_{T}$ and $T=\E X.$ Then, $S(X) \sim f(\cdot + 1) \dd \pi_{T}$ and $\E S(X) = \frac{\E X^{2}}{T} - 1.$ Moreover,
    \begin{displaymath}
        P_{T}f(2) = \frac{\E S(X)}{T} .
    \end{displaymath}

