[Lemma lem:loop_abelian of arXiv:2605.06887, 'Law of large numbers for activated random walk on villages'] For almost all realizations of the instruction stacks $\zeta, \gamma, \kappa$,  the scaled jump odometer configuration $m_*^{(n)}$  and the scaled final sleepy particle counter $s_*^{(n)}$ (cf.\ (equation def_eq_M_star_jump of the paper)) satisfy
\begin{equation}
\phi^{(n)}( m_*^{(n)}) = m_*^{(n)}, \qquad s^{(n)}(m_*^{(n)})=s_*^{(n)}.
\end{equation}

[Prop eqn:sol.sde2 of arXiv:2411.02033, 'Two stochastic versions of the Arps curve decline'] The solution of Equation~((eqn:sde2 of the paper)) is:
\begin{equation}
\forall t \geqslant 0 , \quad Q_t = q_0 (1+bd_0t)^{-1/b} \exp\left( -\frac{1}{2}\sigma^2 t + \sigma B_t \right) .
\end{equation}

[Cor 3.3 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let $\tau$ be a finite stopping time, i.e., $P(\tau<+\infty)=1$, and let $\rho,\mu\in{\mathbb R}$ and $\nu\in{\mathbb R}_+$ be three given constants satisfying $\rho> \mu+\frac{1}{2}\nu^2$. Assume that the generator $g$ satisfies
\begin{enumerate}
\renewcommand{(A3)}{(H1c)}
\renewcommand{(A3)}{(A3)}
\item $\displaystyle \mathbb{E}\left[\int_0^\tau e^{2\rho s} |g(s,0,0)|^2{\rm d}s\right]<+\infty$
\end{enumerate}
and assumptions (A:H2 of the paper)-(A:H5 of the paper) with $\mu_\cdot\equiv \mu$ and $\nu_\cdot\equiv \nu$. Then, for each $\xi\in L_\tau^2(\rho;{\mathbb R}^k)$, BSDE (equation BSDE1.1 of the paper) admits a unique weighted $L^2$ solution $(y_t,z_t)_{t\in[0,\tau]}$ in the space of $H_\tau^2(\rho;{\mathbb R}^{k}\times{\mathbb R}^{k\times d})$. Moreover, we have
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\left[\int_0^{\tau}e^{2 \rho s}|y_s|^2{\rm d}s\right]<+\infty.
\end{align*}

