{"artifact_digest":"sha256:dec61bd535f00356ef830f2efd216db4170a8b2b641eea3224300cd17e0e4215","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/de/dec61bd535f00356ef830f2efd216db4170a8b2b641eea3224300cd17e0e4215.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:1eb7a8bfc2e4a332bf9052b22e878cdd11302a0c88e6608fc05c98a7ade637dc","bundle_entry_key":"2605-16162-lemma-26-haar-zero-integral","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_024","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_024.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-16162-lemma-26-haar-zero-integral","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Choose $D$ a $ 3\times 3$ diagonal matrix with a $-1$ entry in the $i$th row and a $-1$ and $1$ entry in the other two rows. Then $D \in \mrm{SO}(3)$, so by right invariance of the Haar measure,
    \begin{equs}            \E\bigg[(Q_1)_{i,j} \prod_{(a,b) \in P} \mrm{Tr}(Q_a Q_b^T)^{\ell_{(a,b)}}\bigg] &= \E\bigg[(Q_1 D)_{i,j} \prod_{(a,b) \in P} \mrm{Tr}(Q_a D D^T Q_b^T)^{\ell_{(a,b)}}\bigg]\\
    &=-\E\bigg[(Q_1)_{i,j} \prod_{(a,b) \in P} \mrm{Tr}(Q_a Q_b^T)^{\ell_{(a,b)}}\bigg]
    \end{equs}
