\begin{eqnarray*}
 X_1 &=& \sum_{l=1}^k v_{2l-1},\;  X_2 = \sum_{l=1}^k v_{2l}
\end{eqnarray*}
Notice that $\tau_{2k}=X_1+X_2$, where $X_1 \sim Erlang(k,\lambda_{12})$ and $X_2 \sim Erlang(k,\lambda_{21})$. \\
The probability distribution of the sum of two independent Erlang random variables with different shape and rate parameters, or equivalently the sum of independent exponential random variables with different rates,  has been found in [paganis] or in [levyedmond] for example. Adapting their results, specifically  Corollary 6.3 in [levyedmond], to our case we have:
\begin{eqnarray*}
