[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2607.09575, 'Probabilistic estimates for a system of\\noisy integrate-and-fire neurons'] For any set $S \in \mathcal{B}(\R)$, $i = 1,\ldots,N$, and $\delta > 0$ sufficiently close to $0$, we have
	\begin{equation*}
		\prob\left[X_t^i \in S, X_t^i < 0\right] \le C t^{-\frac{\delta}{2}}\left[1 + \sum_{k \ge 1}\prob\left[\tau_k^i \le t\right]^\delta\right]\operatorname{Leb}(S)^{\delta},
	\end{equation*}
	where $C > 0$ is a constant that depends on $p,\,T,\,\mathfrak{K},\,\pref$, the initial distribution $X_0$, and the bounds on $b$ and $\sigma$, but is independent of $i$ and $N$.

