[Proposition 89 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Consider a variational datum satisfying Assumptions \ref{Assumption_A} and \ref{Assumption_B}. Suppose that for any $g,h \in [H]$, we have $\theta_{g,h} \geq 0$ and there exists a constant $c > 0$ such that $V_h''(x) > c > 0$ for any $x \in (\hat{a}_h',\hat{b}_h')$. Then, for each $h \in [H]$ either the $h$-th segment is void or saturated, or the following properties simultaneously hold:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] $\mu_h$ has at least one band;
\item[(ii)] the support of $\mu_h$ is connected;
\item[(iii)] if there is a void, it cannot be reduced to an interior point of the $h$-th segment;
\item[(iv)] the property 2., the lower bound in 4., and the property 5. of Assumption~\ref{Assumption_C} hold.
\end{itemize}
The constants in (iv) depend on the constants in the assumptions and on a positive lower bound for the length of the bands. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem permutation_increases_number_of_holes of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Let $\pi$ denote the swap operators corresponding to a permutation of $\mathbb{Z}$ that exchanges $a$ and $b$ for some $a < b \in \mathbb{Z}$ and maps all other integers to themselves. Let $\eta$ be a configuration of a single-species TASEP on $\mathbb{Z}$, and let $x \in \{a, \dots, b-1\}$. Suppose that in $\eta$, there are a hole at a site in $\{x+1, \dots, b \}$ and a particle at a site in $\{a, \dots, x \}$. Then, in $\pi(\eta)$, 
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[(i)] the number of holes at sites in $\{a, \dots, x \}$ increases by $1$; 
		\item[(ii)] a hole is moved to site $a$; 
		\item[(iii)] a particle is moved to site $b$.
	\end{itemize}

[Theorem e:condition square-integrable RF of arXiv:2605.22803, 'Persistence of asymptotic variance under transport:\\ from hyperfluctuation to stealthy hy'] Suppose that $Z$ is an invariant $\R^d$-valued random field on $\R^d$, that $\Phi$ is an invariant locally square-integrable random measure, and that $\Psi$ is defined as in~(equation e: definition Psi displacement of the paper). Further, either assume that for some $\vartheta>0$ and strongly log-dominating function $\rho$,
    \begin{equation}
        \BE_0^\Phi[\Phi(B_\vartheta) \|Z(0)\|^d \rho(\|Z(0\|))] <\infty,
    \end{equation}
    or assume that $Z$ and $\Phi$ are independent and that
    \begin{equation}
        \BE[\|Z(0)\|^d] < \infty.
    \end{equation}
    Then $\Psi$ is also locally square-integrable.
    \begin{proof}
        The assertion is a simple specialization of Theorem~(t:main square-integrable of the paper) to the special case of displacement kernels with an application of Proposition~(p:independent square-integrable of the paper) to obtain Condition~(c:condition square-integrable general of the paper) from~(equation e:condition square-integrable RF of the paper).
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:subgaussian-directional-tensor-moments of arXiv:2608.11084, 'Sharp Frobenius-Norm Concentration for Sample Moment Tensors'] Let \(X\in\mathbb R^d\) be a centered sub-Gaussian random vector with
covariance matrix \(\Sigma\) and sub-Gaussian constant \(K\), and let
\(p\ge2\) be an integer. Then, for every \(q\ge1\),
\[
\sup_{\|A\|_{\mathsf F}=1}
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\|
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\langle
A,X^{\otimes p}-\mathbbm{E} X^{\otimes p}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rangle_{\mathsf F}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\|_{L_q}
\lesssim_p
K^p \begin{cases}
\|\Sigma\|_{\mathsf F}^{p/2}+\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2},
& p \text{ even},\\[3pt]
\|\Sigma\|_{\mathsf F}^{(p-1)/2}\|\Sigma\|^{1/2}\sqrt q+\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2},
& p \text{ odd}.
\end{cases}
\]
 Moreover, if \(X\) is Gaussian, then, for every \(q\ge1\),
\[
\sup_{\|A\|_{\mathsf F}=1}
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\|
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\langle
A,X^{\otimes p}-\mathbbm{E} X^{\otimes p}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rangle_{\mathsf F}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\|_{L_q}
\asymp_p
\begin{cases}
\|\Sigma\|_{\mathsf F}^{p/2-1}\|\Sigma\| q
+
\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2},
& p \text{ even},\\[3pt]
\|\Sigma\|_{\mathsf F}^{(p-1)/2}\|\Sigma\|^{1/2}\sqrt q
+
\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2},
& p \text{ odd},
\end{cases}
\]
and 
\[
\sup_{\|A\|_{\mathsf F}=1}
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\|
\mathopen{}\mathclose\bgroup\originalleft\langle
A,X^{\otimes p}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\rangle_{\mathsf F}
\aftergroup\egroup\originalright\|_{L_q}
\asymp_p
\begin{cases}
\|\Sigma\|_{\mathsf F}^{p/2}
+
\|\Sigma\|^{p/2}q^{p/2},
& p \text{ even},\\[3pt]
\|\Sigma\|_{\mathsf F}^{(p-1)/2}\|\Sigma\|^{1/2}\sqrt q
+
