\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\Lp(\cA_{\sigma,m,L})
&\ge \sup_{s\ge0}\left\{\inf_{x\in[-L,L]}
\left(\frac{q(x)s}{\sigma}-a(x)\right)-\frac{M(s)-1}{\sigma^m}\right\}\\
&\ge \sigma^{-m}\cH(q_*\sigma^{m-1})-\max a .
\end{aligned}

\end{equation}
The small- and large-argument asymptotics of $\cH$ in Theorem~\ref{thm:heteroHamiltonian} yield the required lower limits.

We turn to the upper bounds. Let $x_0\in[-L,L]$ satisfy $q(x_0)=q_*$. In each regime we choose ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:9e1777136eea6332f92fb01da49e047ac14fcdbc2903ff1b88d146f888229438","revision_digest":"sha256:efb14c9fc24faae9fa2e36b7c04d0f6e2101808974f4465cd4a0b84df6d7e001","source_id":"arxiv:2609.02416","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

