[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Let $p\geq 2$ and~\eqref{co:1} and~\eqref{co:5} hold. Then pathwise uniqueness holds for~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model}, and any two solutions $I$ and $\tilde{I}$ to~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model} satisfy
\begin{equation*}
\E\big[|I_{t} - \tilde{I}_{t}|^{p}\big] \leq e^{\int_{0}^{t}\overline{\lambda}_{p}(s,N(s))\,\mathrm{d}s}\E\big[|I_{0} - \tilde{I}_{0}|^{p}\big]
\end{equation*}
for all $t\geq 0$ with $\overline{\lambda}_{p} := p(\hat{b}_{k+1} + \hat{\lambda}_{k+1} + c_{p}\lambda^{2})$. In particular, the integrability of $\overline{\lambda}_{p}^{+}(\cdot,N)$ entails that $\sup_{t\geq 0}\E[|I_{t} - \tilde{I}_{t}|^{p}] < \infty$. In this case,
\begin{equation*}
\int_{0}^{\infty}\overline{\lambda}_{p}^{-}(s,N(s))\,\mathrm{d}s = \infty\quad\text{implies}\quad \lim_{t\uparrow\infty} \E\big[|I_{t} - \tilde{I}_{t}|^{p}\big] = 0.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:parisi:ftl:reduce of arXiv:2507.06522, 'Balanced multi-species spin glasses'] Assume (equation delta_decay of the paper) and (equation balanced of the paper).
Given a sequence $q = (0 = q_0 \leqslant q_1 \leqslant \cdots \leqslant q_k \leqslant q_{k+1} = 1)$, let $\wh{{\boldsymbol q}} = (\wh{{\boldsymbol q}}_j)_{j\in\{0,\dots,k+1\}}$ be given by $\wh{{\boldsymbol q}}_j = q_j\cdot{\boldsymbol 1}$ for each $j$.
For either ${\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}\in \{\mathsf{Ising},\mathsf{spherical}\}$ and any sequence $m = (0 = m_0 < m_1 < \cdots < m_k = 1)$, we have
\eeq{ 
    \mathscr{P}_{{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}(m,\wh{{\boldsymbol q}})=\mathscr{P}^\mathsf{single}_{{\scaleobj{1.1}{\diamond}}}(m,q).
}

