	\(\kappa_2b_{10}-(1-\theta_2)b_{20}\le0\), then \(Y\) reaches zero in finite
	time.  If \(\kappa_2b_{10}-(1-\theta_2)b_{20}>0\) and
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{x^{\kappa_2}}{\kappa_2b_{10}-(1-\theta_2)b_{20}}
		\exp\left(\frac{\kappa_2a_1y^{\kappa_1}}{\kappa_1b_{20}}\right)
		<\frac{y^{1-\theta_2}}{(1-\theta_2)a_2},

