		then \(Y\) never reaches zero.   On the other hand, if 
	\(\kappa_2b_{10}-(1-\theta_2)b_{20}>0\) and
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{x^{\kappa_2}}{\kappa_2b_{10}-(1-\theta_2)b_{20}}
		>\frac{y^{1-\theta_2}}{(1-\theta_2)a_2},

	\end{equation}
	then \(Y\) reaches zero in finite time. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

