[Prop key prop uniqueness full space of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] For every $0<\beta'<\beta$,
\begin{equation}
\langle \tau_0 \tau_{\mathbf{e}_1} \rangle^+_{\beta'}\leq \langle \tau_0 \tau_{\mathbf{e}_1} \rangle_{\beta},
\end{equation}
where $\mathbf{e}_1=(1,0,\ldots,0)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem:P-sharp-lower of arXiv:2608.12147, 'The Average Singular Value of a Complex Gaussian Random Matrix Strictly Decreases with Dim'] For $N\geqslant3$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
 P_N\geqslant \frac1{3(N+1)}\Bigg[&A_0-\frac1{\pi(2N-1)}
 +\frac{W_{1,N}}{2N+1}
 +\frac{W_{2,N}}{(2N+1)^2}\Bigg],
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where
\begin{align}
\mathcal{H}_N^* & := \frac8{15}+\frac12\log\frac{2N+1}{7},\nonumber \\
W_{1,N}& := \frac1\pi\left(\mathcal{H}_N^*+\frac16-\frac1{2(2N+1)}\right),
\\ 
W_{2,N}& := \frac1\pi\left(\frac{N-1}{2}+\mathcal{H}_N^*-\frac1{12}+\frac1{4(2N+1)}\right).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition def:filtration-function of arXiv:2608.29719, 'Persistence Pairing Graphs: Tracking Changes of Selected Homology Bases'] A \emph{filtration function} is a map $f:\mathcal K\longrightarrow\mathbb R$ such that
\begin{equation}

\tau\subseteq\overline{\sigma} \quad\Longrightarrow\quad f(\tau)\leq f(\sigma)
\end{equation}
for all cells $\sigma,\tau\in\mathcal K$.

