body:
[Proposition prop:harmonic-grad-c3 of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] Under (lem:tailrl-regularity of the paper), for every $T\geq1$,
\begin{equation}
\nabla_\theta J_{\mathrm{TailRL{}}}^{(T)}(\theta;x)
=
\sum_{k=1}^{T}
\frac{1}{k}
\nabla_\theta\text{Best-of-}k(\theta;x).

\end{equation}
Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
\nabla_\theta J_{\mathrm{TailRL{}}}^{(T)}(\theta;x)
=
\int_0^1
\frac{1-\left(1-p_\theta(x,\tau)\right)^T}
{p_\theta(x,\tau)}
\nabla_\theta p_\theta(x,\tau)
\,d\tau,

\end{equation}
where the ratio is interpreted by continuity as $T$ when $p_\theta(x,\tau)=0$.

