[Lemma lemma_uniform_bound_time_Omega of arXiv:2411.16452, 'Interface scaling limit for the critical planar Ising model perturbed by a magnetic field'] Let $t \in (0,\infty)$. There almost surely exist $m_0 \geq 1$ and a sequence $(C_{k,t})_k$ such that, almost surely, for any $m \geq m_0$ and any $k \geq 1$,
\begin{equation*}
    \sum_{(x_1,\dots,x_k) \in \Omega_{m,t}} \delta_m^{\frac{15k}{8}}\vert \EEpmtime{m}{t}[\sigma_{x_1} \dots \sigma_{x_k}] \vert \leq C_{k,t}
\end{equation*}
with $\sum_k\frac{h^k}{k!}C_{k,t} < \infty$ almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

