[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2604.07207, 'Mixing times of step-reinforced random walks'] Under Assumption \ref{mainassum}, if $\mu$ is symmetric, then for any $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$,
       \begin{equation}

 t^{(\alpha)}_{\mathrm{mix}}(\varepsilon) \leq  \frac{C}{1-\alpha} \log \left(\frac{|G|}{\varepsilon}\right) \frac{1}{\gamma_*},
    \end{equation}
   where $\gamma_*$ is the absolute spectral gap of $P_{\mu}$, and $C$ is a positive absolute constant that does not depend on $G,\mu, \alpha$ and $\varepsilon$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

