[Corollary cor:RGP-scalar of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The one-point Fredholm determinant
$F_{t, a, n} = \det(I - K_{t, a, n})$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
q F_{t, a, n+1} F_{t-1, a+2, n}
- F_{t-1, a+1, n} F_{t, a+1, n+1}
+ p F_{t, a+1, n} F_{t-1, a+1, n+1}
= 0,
\end{equation}
at every $(t, a, n)$ with $t \ge 1$ and
$a < h_{n+1}(t{-}1) - 1$.

[Corollary corollary7.3 of arXiv:2608.01279, 'Stochastic heat equation with nondegenerate Hölder diffusion coefficient: uniqueness below'] Lemma (lemmas7.1 of the paper) and (lemmas7.2 of the paper) imply that, for every fixed \(t>0\),

\begin{equation}
r_s(U(t)-V^n(t))\longrightarrow0
\quad\hbox{in probability}.

\end{equation}

