body:
[Prop gPI-char of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] The gPI constant $\alpha_{\gPI}$ defined in~(equation def:PI-LSI-con of the paper) is continuous on $\mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$. Moreover, we have the following alternative characterisations for any $\zeta \in \mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})$
    \begin{align}
        \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta) 
        = \inf_{\substack{f\in \langle \1 \rangle^{\perp_\zeta} \\ \|f\|_\zeta=1}}\mathscr{E}_\zeta(f)
        = \inf_{\substack{f\in \langle \1 \rangle^\perp \\ \|f\|=1}} 
        \frac{\mathscr{E}_\zeta(f)}{\operatorname{var}_\zeta(f)}  
        .
     \end{align}
    In addition, for any $\mathcal{P}_+(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}) \ni \zeta_\varepsilon \to \zeta$ and any $0 < \delta_\varepsilon \to 0$ as $\varepsilon \to 0$, we have
    \begin{align}
        \alpha_{\gPI}(\zeta) 
        = 
        \frac12 \lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} \inf_{\substack{\varphi \in \mathcal D_{\zeta_\varepsilon}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}) \\ 0 < \| \varphi - \1 \|_{\zeta_\varepsilon} < \delta_\varepsilon }}
\frac{\mathscr{R}_{\zeta_\varepsilon}(\varphi)}{\mathscr{H}_{\zeta_\varepsilon}(\varphi)}.
     \end{align}

[Theorem th1 of arXiv:2412.04973, 'On the Laplace equation with non-local dynamical boundary conditions'] Let $l > 0.$ Then there is an Hilbert basis $\{\varphi_n, n\in  {\mathbb N}\}$ of $L^2(\Gamma)$, $\varphi_n\in \mathcal{D}(\Gamma),$  $\varphi_n$ real valued, and an increasing real sequence $\{\lambda_n,
n\in  {\mathbb N}\}$,   $\lambda_n\to\infty $  as $ n\to\infty,$ each $\lambda_n$ having finite multiplicity, such that for any $n\in {\mathbb N}$ a unique solution  $\psi_n$  (which belongs to $C^\infty(\bar\Omega )$
of the Dirichlet non-homogeneous problem

\begin{align}

\left\lbrace
\begin{array}{ll}
\displaystyle \Delta \psi_n=0 \qquad
&\text{in
$\Omega$,}\\
\psi_n(x)=\varphi_n(x)&\text{on $\Gamma$}
\end{array}
\right.
\end{align}
solves the eigenvalue problem
\begin{align}

