[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2511.13404, 'Asymptotic stability and mean ergodicity of Feller processes on Polish spaces'] Let $\{\xi_t\}_{t\ge 0}$ be a family of random variables and $g:\R_+\rightarrow\R_+$ satisfying $\lim\limits_{a\to\infty}g(a)/a=\infty$. If 
    \begin{equation}
        \sup_{t\ge0}\E(g(|\xi_t|))<\infty,
    \end{equation}
then $\{\xi_t\}_{t\ge 0}$ is uniformly integrable. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

