body:
[Corollary cor:bw of arXiv:2607.06249, 'Extreme least singular values of Gaussian row submatrices and a phase retrieval stability '] Let $A_m\in\mathbb{R}^{(2m-1)\times m}$ have independent standard Gaussian entries. Then
\begin{equation}
  \frac{1}{m}\log\omega(A_m)\xrightarrow{P}-\log4,
\end{equation}
with the rate
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}\left\{\left|\frac{1}{m}\log\omega(A_m)+\log4\right|>\varepsilon\right\}=O_\varepsilon(m^{-1})
\end{equation}
for every fixed $\varepsilon>0$. Equivalently, $\omega(A_m)=4^{-m+o_P(m)}$.

Let $R_m=\max_{1\le i\le 2m-1}\|a_i\|$. For every $b>1/4$, $\mathbb{P}\{\omega(A_m)\le R_m b^m\}\to1$. For
every $b<1/4$ and every fixed $C<\infty$, $\mathbb{P}\{\omega(A_m)\le C R_m b^m\}\to0$. Thus the Gaussian
critical base in the Balan--Wang question is $1/4$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

