[Proposition prop:negligible W- of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] {Recall $t_{\mu/n}=\argmin_{t \in (0,2)}\lambda_{\mu/n}(t)$, and} let $X_{n,m}$ be defined as in~(equation eq:def smt of the paper), and $\epsilon_n\ll1$ be such that $\epsilon_nt_{\mu/n}\gg1$ and $\epsilon_n^2(\mu^2n)^{1/3}\gg\log(\mu^2n)$.
