[Lemma lem:TV-llr of arXiv:2601.07045, 'From Continuous to Discrete: \\ a No-U-Turn Sampler for Permutations'] Let $p$ and $q$ be probability mass functions on a finite set $\mathcal{I}$ such that
\[
  e^{-\varepsilon}
  \;\le\;
  \frac{q(t)}{p(t)}
  \;\le\;
  e^{\varepsilon}
