[Proposition 27 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] [Variational formula for entropy] 

      Let $(\Omega, \mathcal{F},\mu)$ be a probability space, and let $f : \Omega \rightarrow (0,\infty) $ be a $\mu$--integrable function such that $\int_{\Omega} f \dd \mu = 1.$ Then 
      \begin{displaymath}
          \Ent_{ \mu } (f) = \sup_{g} \Big\{ \int f g \dd \mu - \log \Big( \int e^{g} \dd \mu \Big) \Big\}
      \end{displaymath}
      where the supremum is taken over measurable and bounded functions $g : \Omega \rightarrow \R.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

