[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2606.14170, 'Uniform-in-time error estimates for McKean-Vlasov SDEs with common noise and stochastic al'] Suppose that Assumptions \ref{A1}, \ref{S1} and \ref{N1} hold with $\lambda_1>2\lambda_2$, for any $p>0$, $i\in\mathbb{S}_N$ and $\delta\in(0,\frac{1}{2(\lambda_1-2\lambda_2)})$, there is a constant $C>0$ such that 
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}|\widetilde X_t^{i,N}|^p\le \mathbb{E}|\widetilde X_0^{i,N}|^p+C, ~t\ge 0,
\end{align}
in case of $\mathbb{E}|\widetilde X_0^{i,N}|^p<\infty$.

