[Lemma 7 (Markov property) of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Suppose that~$x_1,\dots,x_m\in\T_n$ are vertices such that the subtrees $\T^{(1)},\dots,\T^{(m)}$ of~$\T_n$ rooted at these vertices are vertex-disjoint. Write~$n_i$ for the depth of~$\T^{(i)}$ and denote
\begin{equation}

\V(x_1,\dots,x_m):=\{x_1,\dots,x_m\}\cup\Bigl(\T_n\smallsetminus\bigcup_{i=1}^m\T^{(i)}\Bigr).
\end{equation}
Then, for   all   $t>0$, conditional on $\{L_t(x)\colon x\in\V(x_1,\dots,x_m)\}$, the families
\begin{equation}

\{L_t(x)\colon x\in\T^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^m
\end{equation}
are independent with the~$i$-th family distributed as $\{L_u(x)\colon x\in\T_{n_i}\}$ for~$u:=L_t(x_i)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem noexcursion of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] Let $n$ be a $\sigma$-finite positive measure on $\mathcal{E}_\infty$ such that  \begin{equation} 
\begin{aligned}
n\big(X_{t+s}\in & \, \mathrm{d} y, 0<t+s<\sigma_{x_0}^{-}<\zeta\big)\\
&=\int_{[0,\infty]}n(X_t\in \mathrm{d} x, t<\sigma_{x_0}^{-}<\zeta)\mathbb{P}_x(X_s^{\mathrm{m}}\in \mathrm{d} y, s<\sigma_{x_0}^{-}<\zeta),
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
n(1\wedge \zeta)<\infty,
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
n(X_t\in \mathrm{d} x, t<\zeta)\underset{t\rightarrow 0}{\rightarrow} \delta_\infty \text{ weakly},
\end{equation}

Then, if $\underline{\theta}_{\,\scriptscriptstyle\Phi,\hat{\Sigma}}>1$, we have 
\[n(\exists s\in (0,\zeta): X_s<\infty)=0.\]

