[Definition of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] An abstract operator algebra, or $C^*$-algebra, is a complex algebra $A$ having a norm $||.||$ and an involution $*$, subject to the following conditions:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $A$ is closed with respect to the norm.

\item We have $||aa^*||=||a||^2$, for any $a\in A$.
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma 13 (Thin boundary-layer volume) of arXiv:2607.19752, 'Weak Equilibrium Measures and Capacity--Hitting Identities\\ for the Hypoelliptic Third-Or'] Let $\Sigma\in\{\partial A,\partial B,\partial\calD\}$ and let
$K_1\subset\R^{3d}$ be compact.  There exist constants $a_0,b_0,C>0$ such that,
for $0<a\le a_0$ and $0<b\le b_0$,
\[
    \operatorname{Leb}\left\{
        y\in K_1:\dist(y,\Sigma)\le a,\ |r(y)|\le b
    \right\}
    \le C a b^d .
\]

[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.29554, 'Limiting Behavior of a Class of Hermitian Yang--Mills Metrics, II: Exponential Approximati'] For any nonnegative integer $k$, there exist constants $C_k,c_k>0$, independent of $\epsilon$, such that for all sufficiently small $\epsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}
\left\|\Lambda_{\omega_\epsilon}\Theta(H_{0,\epsilon})\right\|_{C^k}\leq C_ke^{-c_k/\epsilon}.

\end{equation}

[Proposition prop:bridge_subg_tail of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $B^{(n)}_x=(B^{(n)}_{x;t}:0\leq t \leq n)$ be a uniform bridge of length $n$ ending at $x$, that is a uniform element from $\mathcal B^{(n)}_x$.
    Then, for any $A>0$, there exists $R_1,R_2>0$ such that, for any $|x|\leq A\sqrt{n}$ and $T\geq0$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        \Prob{\frac{w\big(B^{(n)}_x\big)}{\sqrt{n}}>T}\leq R_1e^{-R_2T^2}\,.
    \end{align*}

