[Lemma vanishing of arXiv:2604.17253, 'Large Deviations for the Nonlinear Schrödinger Equation with Randomized Quasi-Periodic Ini'] Let \(N\sim\varepsilon^{-\frac1\nu+\mu_1}\) be defined by (equation eq:N of the paper), and let \(\delta\) be as in (cor:polynomial_decay of the paper). Then, for every \(\omega\notin\Omega_\delta\),
\begin{align}
\mathscr R_N
=
\mathcal O\!\left(
\varepsilon^{-\frac12+\frac{\mu_2}2}
\right).
\end{align}

