[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2605.23222, 'On global solutions to the semidiscrete stochastic heat equation'] Let $\beta$ be so small that the conclusions of Theorems~\ref{thm:factorization} and~\ref{thm:continuous_Talagrand} hold. Then for $y$ fixed we have the following convergence statements:

\begin{equation} 
\lvert B(y,t) \rvert \xrightarrow[t \to \infty]{} 0 \; \text{ in probability},
\end{equation}

\begin{equation} 
C(y,t)  \xrightarrow[t \to \infty]{} 0  \; \text{ in probability}.
