[Lemma LEM:BM of arXiv:2412.09790, 'Critical threshold for weakly interacting log-correlated focusing Gibbs measures'] Let $\mu$ be as in (equation gauss0 of the paper).
Then, we have 
\begin{align*}
\mu \bigg(\int_{\mathbb{T}^d}:\!  u^2    \!: dx = K\bigg) = 0
\end{align*}

\noindent
for any $K \in \mathbb{R}$, 
where $\int_{\mathbb{T}^d} :\!u^2\!: dx$ is the limit of 
$\int_{\mathbb{T}^d} :\!(\pi_N u)^2\!:dx$
as $N \to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

