body:
[Lem proofthm3i of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] There exists $x_0\in (0,\infty)$ such that for all $a\in [x_0,\infty)$, 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}_\infty[\sigma^{\mathrm{e}\infty,-}_a]\leq \frac{2}{1-\overline{\theta}_{\,\scriptscriptstyle\Phi, \hat{\Sigma}}}\int_a^{\infty}\frac{\mathrm{d} u}{\hat{\Sigma}(u)}.\end{equation}
In particular, $\infty$ is non-absorbing and instantaneous.

