[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2506.22020, 'Norm-dependent Lamperti-type MAP representations of stable processes and Brownian motions '] Let $(\xi,\Xi)=(\xi_t,\Xi_t)_{t\geq0}$ be the underlying MAP of $Z$ from (\ref{item_a}) with respect to $\|\cdot\|_1$. The killing rate of $(\xi,\Xi)$ is given by
	\begin{equation}
		q(\boldsymbol{x})=\mathbbm{1}_{(0,\infty)^d}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\alpha}\sum_{k=1}^d \frac{\Gamma(1+\alpha)\sin(\pi\alpha(1-\rho_k))}{\pi} \Big(\frac{x_k}{\|\boldsymbol{x}\|_1}\Big)^{-\alpha},\quad \boldsymbol{x}=(x_1,\ldots,x_d)\in(0,\infty)^d,

