[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] There exists a constant $C>0$, depending only on $\omega$, such that for any $N\in\N^+$ and $f\in H^1(\omega;\R^2)$,
	\begin{equation}
	\|(I-\mathsf P_N)f\|_{L^2(\omega)}\leq C\lambda_{N+1}^{-1/4}\|f\|_{H^1(\omega)},
	\end{equation}
    where $\mathsf P_N$ denotes the orthogonal projection in $L^2(\omega;\R^2)$ onto ${\rm span}\{\psi_j:1\leq j\leq N\}$.

