		\begin{equation*}
			\frac{1}{\sigma^{d}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}} f(x) \, \hat{\xi}(\mathrm{d}x) = \frac{1}{\sigma^{d}}\hat{\xi}([\sigma a, \sigma b])
		\end{equation*}
        Since $\xi$ is ergodic, Thorisson's shift-coupling lemma [Kallenberg2017] yields the existence of a random variable $T$ for which 
        \begin{equation*}
            \hat{\xi}\stackrel{(d)}{=} \xi-T.
        \end{equation*}
        Consequently,
        \begin{equation*}
